node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
# Never commit a real environment file. .env.example is the checked-in template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Where the filesystem object store writes in development. Uploaded document
# bytes are not source, and 32 of them reached the index once because the store
# was pointed at a URL and `git add -A` swept up the result.
.data/
# Belt and braces: if the store is ever pointed at a URL again, the directory it
# creates is named after the scheme and must not be committed either.
http:/
https:/

# Held back from the public repository by owner decision (20 August 2026).
# READINESS-REVIEW.md itemises every unfixed security weakness — unencrypted
# secrets, an existence oracle, untuned limits — and on a public repo that is a
# map for anyone who finds a deployment. It lives on disk and is shared
# directly until the gaps it lists are closed.
**/docs/READINESS-REVIEW.md
# Held back for the same reason as the readiness review: this repository is
# public, and both documents enumerate what the system cannot yet do. The
# owner's call, not a default.
**/docs/MASTER-COMMAND-WEB-PORTAL-BACKEND.html
**/docs/MASTER-COMMAND-WEB-PORTAL-BACKEND.pdf
**/docs/CERTIFICATION-WEB-PORTAL-BACKEND.html
**/docs/CERTIFICATION-WEB-PORTAL-BACKEND.pdf

# Uploaded bytes from the development server. Never a deliverable.
.dev-objects/

# Service-account keys. Firebase, Google Cloud, anything shaped like them.
#
# `scan-secrets.py` already refuses a PEM private-key header, so a committed one
# fails the gate — this is the earlier stop, before it is staged at all. Added
# 2026-08-30 after a Firebase admin key reached a place it should not have; the
# key itself was rotated rather than trusted to stay unread.
#
# The marker is described rather than written out: spelling it here made the
# scanner flag this very file, which is the trap of a gate tripping over its own
# explanation.
*-adminsdk-*.json
service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
firebase-*.json

# The five patterns above carry `**/` since the monorepo move on 2026-08-30.
# A pattern written `docs/x` is anchored to the directory holding the
# .gitignore, so when the service moved to apps/ebpco-api/ they silently
# stopped matching and five deliberately-unversioned documents became
# untracked. Anchored patterns are the quiet casualty of moving a tree.

# The portal service's dependencies and build, same as the API's.
apps/castilla-portal/node_modules/
apps/castilla-portal/dist/
